# A pro-cyclic profinite group is a quotient of `Ẑ`

This file proves `NK.TameStructure.ProCyclic.exists_continuous_surjective_zhat_of_isProCyclic`:
a compact, Hausdorff, totally disconnected topological group `H` all of whose finite quotients are
cyclic (`NK.LocalTame.IsProCyclic H`) admits a continuous surjection `Ẑ ↠ H` from the profinite
completion `Ẑ = NK.LocalAnabelian.Zhat` of `ℤ`.

## The mathematics

Since `H` is pro-cyclic, it is topologically generated by a single element
(`NK.TameStructure.ProCyclic.exists_topologicallyCyclic_of_isProCyclic`): there is `g : H`
whose image generates every finite quotient `H ⧸ N`.

For such a `g`, the assignments `k ↦ (gN) ^ k` on the dense copy of `ℤ` inside `Ẑ` define
homomorphisms `famHom g N : Ẑ →* H ⧸ N` (see `NK.TameStructure.ProCyclic.Defs`).  These are
compatible: for `M ≤ N` the transition map `H ⧸ M →* H ⧸ N` sends `gM ↦ gN`, and since the copy
of `ℤ` is dense and the quotients are Hausdorff, the two composites `Ẑ →* H ⧸ N` coincide.

In a profinite group the open normal subgroups have trivial intersection and form a fundamental
system of neighbourhoods of `1`.  Hence the two lemmas

* `eq_of_forall_mk'_eq` (an element is determined by its images in all finite quotients), and
* `exists_mk'_eq_famHom` (a family of compatible prescribed images is realised by an element, by
  compactness),

produce a well-defined element `phiFun g z ∈ H` for every `z : Ẑ`, and `phiHom g` is a group
homomorphism `Ẑ →* H`.  It is continuous because each composite `Ẑ → H ⧸ N` is.  Finally, each
`famHom g N` is surjective, so the image of `phiHom g` meets every coset of every open normal
subgroup; it is therefore dense, and being closed (a continuous image of the compact `Ẑ` inside
the Hausdorff `H`) it is all of `H`.

## Main definitions and results

* `NK.TameStructure.ProCyclic.phiFun` — the underlying function `Ẑ → H`;
* `NK.TameStructure.ProCyclic.phiHom` — the homomorphism `Ẑ →* H`;
* `NK.TameStructure.ProCyclic.exists_continuous_surjective_zhat_of_isProCyclic`.
-/
